    "geometry['graph']: rebuilt from NewMaze (MM_Maze_Utils.py) plus an entrance node",
    "environment: declared binary-tree labyrinth, the repository's track graph with each dead end extended half a cell to its end wall (MazeWall) (Rosenberg et al. 2021 repository NewMaze (MM_Maze_Utils.py): corridors one cell apart; the paper: 'corridors (1-1/8 inches wide)' on a 1.5 inch grid); tracked point: the nose (the repository's trajectory keypoints); physical width 1 units (chosen: the corridor pitch, so a corridor's footprint ends at the wall it shares with its neighbour; the paper's corridors are 1-1/8 in on a 1.5 in grid, 0.75 cell, at which 13% of nose samples fall outside), 2.0% of samples beyond half of it (5% at 0-1 units/s, 1% at 1-inf units/s); placement tolerance 1.06 units (track_width: twice the samples' 99% quantile distance from the track, at least the physical width and one bin; a tracked head swings past an unwalled track's edge, so 1.0% of samples are dropped by construction); placement: the maze cells of the repository's own alignment (authors' graph); fit: median |lateral offset| 0.14 units, worst stretch bias 0.49 units (limit 0.5), worst unsupported share of a segment 4%; track length 207.0 units"
